          "description": {
            "comment": "The spotted minute salamander (Thorius spilogaster) is a species of salamander in the family Plethodontidae. It is endemic to Mexico and only known from the south and southeast flanks of Pico de Orizaba in central Veracruz, at elevations of 2,500-2,725 m (8,202-8,940 ft) above sea level (from Wikipedia entry). This sample of an individual found in Veracruz, Mexico was procured by Sean Rovito to generate a high-quality reference genome for the Vertebrate Genomes Project (VGP). Sequencing and genome assembly were conducted at the Vertebrate Genome Lab (VGL) at the Rockefeller University, led by Erich D. Jarvis, Giulio Formenti, and Jennifer Balacco.",
